{"about_the_game":"Pixel Puzzles World War II, merging history with the definitive jigsaw puzzler on the PC platform.<br><br>The Blitz refers to the sustained aerial bombing campaign conducted by Nazi Germany against the United Kingdom during World War II, primarily from September 1940 to May 1941. The Blitz was characterized by relentless nighttime air raids, which aimed to demoralize and weaken British civilians and infrastructure. Cities like London, Coventry, and Liverpool suffered extensive damage, and many thousands of civilians were killed or injured. Despite the devastation, the British people displayed remarkable resilience and courage, as they endured the Blitz with the help of air raid shelters, evacuation efforts, and the heroism of the Royal Air Force, eventually emerging victorious against the threat of invasion.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">PACK INFO:</h2><strong>Puzzle Count:</strong> 24<br><strong>Total Piece Count:</strong> 5622<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">PACK CONTENTS:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>A Bus In Harrington Square - x425<br></li><li>Anderson Shelter - x140<br></li><li>Bomb Remnants - x216<br></li><li>Chenies Street - x216<br></li><li>Children in East End - x425<br></li><li>Churchill Visits - x330<br></li><li>Crater - x140<br></li><li>Firefighters - x216<br></li><li>Grey Tube Shelter by Henry Moore - x140<br></li><li>Heinkel He 111 Over Wapping - x216<br></li><li>Holland House LIbrary - x216<br></li><li>Necropolis Railway Station - x96<br></li><li>Normal Day - x216<br></li><li>Passing Time in Shelter - x216<br></li><li>Peter Robinson Department Store at Oxford Circus - x330<br></li><li>Pioneer Corps Search Rubble - x96<br></li><li>Rations - x425<br></li><li>Shelters in the Tube by Henry Moore - x140<br></li><li>Sleeping in Shelter - x216<br></li><li>St Paul's Cathedral - x96<br></li><li>Tower Bridge - x140<br></li><li>Tube Shelter - x330<br></li><li>Union Jack - x216<br></li><li>Women's Volunteer Service Breakfast - x425</li></ul>","background":"https://s